# 99-touchbar-dfr.rules — keep GNOME/mutter's hands OFF the T1 Touch Bar DRM card.
#
# MECHANISM
#   systemd's 71-seat.rules tags every drm card with TAG+="seat" and
#   TAG+="master-of-seat"; logind then assigns the device to the seat named in
#   the ID_SEAT udev property (default "seat0" when unset). mutter's native
#   backend enumerates DRM devices through udev and only opens cards whose
#   ID_SEAT matches its session seat (seat0) — both at startup AND on hotplug.
#   So: re-pointing ID_SEAT at a dummy seat ("seat-touchbar", which has no
#   sessions) makes logind file the card under that seat and makes mutter skip
#   it entirely, leaving DRM master free for dfr-render.
#
#   - This rule runs at 99-, i.e. AFTER 71-seat.rules (which adds the tags) and
#     after 73-seat-late.rules; we add TAG+="seat-touchbar" ourselves to mirror
#     what 73-seat-late would have done with this ID_SEAT.
#   - TAG-="master-of-seat" so logind doesn't consider the dummy seat
#     graphics-capable; TAG-="uaccess" since no session will ever sit on it
#     (dfr-render runs as root anyway).
#   - Matching: ATTRS{} walks up the parent chain to the USB device 05ac:8600
#     (the iBridge). The Intel GPU (PCI 8086) has no such USB parent and is
#     untouched.
#
# RELOGIN / ORDERING CAVEAT
#   The rule applies when the card's add/change uevent fires. Mutter does NOT
#   release a card it has already opened, so the rule must be in effect BEFORE
#   the appletbdrm card is created. If the modules were already loaded:
#       sudo udevadm control --reload
#       sudo rmmod apple_dfr_cfgsel appletbdrm && sudo insmod ... (reload both)
#   A relogin/GDM restart is NOT needed when the card is created fresh after
#   the rule is installed (hotplug path). If mutter still grabs it (see
#   DFRD-RUNBOOK.md verification step), log out/in once as the fallback.
#
# INSTALL
#   sudo install -m 0644 99-touchbar-dfr.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", \
  SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="05ac", ATTRS{idProduct}=="8600", \
  ENV{ID_SEAT}="seat-touchbar", TAG+="seat", TAG+="seat-touchbar", \
  TAG-="master-of-seat", TAG-="uaccess"

# OPTIONAL (leave commented unless needed): if hid-generic turns the config-2
# digitizer's non-standard reports into a garbage evdev input device that
# libinput picks up (check `sudo libinput list-devices` while in config 2),
# uncomment to hide it from the desktop. WARNING: this matches the iBridge in
# BOTH configs — with the display stack UNLOADED (stock config 1) it would
# also kill the stock Touch Bar's media-key input. Only enable once the
# display stack is persistent.
#ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", ATTRS{idVendor}=="05ac", \
#  ATTRS{idProduct}=="8600", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
